/* Late ports of the sheet (SOLID stage 10, D and I). Replaces the open bag __R (app/00-reg.js).
   A file that is earlier in the load order than the owner of a name (a function or a value that the owner defines later) used to read it as __R.NAME.
   Now it imports the port from here. The owner binds the name once, at the place where it used to call Object.defineProperty(__R,"NAME",...):
       bindLive("NAME", {get: getter, set: setter})
   The getter reads the owner's variable at the moment of use, so a function that a later patch replaces (renderAll = ...) is seen as before.
   Behavior kept from __R: a read before the owner has bound gives undefined (lateGet), a call before it throws a TypeError, a write before the bind is kept in a plain slot that the bind then drops (as defineProperty did), a write to a bound name needs a setter.
   The same port carries the reads of a data or logic file from a UI file (rGet, renderAll, refreshEntry ...): the low layer imports the port, the UI file binds, so the low layer does not name the UI file (guard_deps).
   Not for a function that a reader passes as a value and that a later patch replaces by a wrapper of itself (bldDot): the port always returns the newest one, so that wrapper would call itself.
   New: a name outside the list below, a second binding of a name, or a write to a name without setter throws. No imports on purpose (loads first). */
